---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Hero from '../../components/Hero.astro';
import ProductGrid from '../../components/ProductGrid.astro';
import FAQAccordion from '../../components/FAQAccordion.astro';
import QuoteForm from '../../components/quote/QuoteForm.tsx';
import { serviceSchema } from '../../lib/schema/service';
import { faqPageSchema } from '../../lib/schema/faqPage';
import { getAllProducts } from '../../data/catalog/shopify';
import '../../styles/quote-form.css';

const allProducts = await getAllProducts();
const products = allProducts.filter((p) => p.tags.includes('ceiling')).slice(0, 9);

const faqs = (await getCollection('faq'))
  .filter((f) => f.data.pages.includes('ceiling'))
  .sort((a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order)
  .map((f) => ({ question: f.data.question, body: f.body.trim() }));

const schemas = [
  serviceSchema({
    name: 'Ceiling balloon installations',
    description:
      'Suspended balloon clusters, canopies, and overhead installations for venues and events in London Ontario.',
    startingPrice: 699,
    url: '/services/ceiling',
  }),
];
if (faqs.length > 0) {
  schemas.push(faqPageSchema(faqs.map((f) => ({ question: f.question, answer: f.body }))));
}
---

<BaseLayout
  topic="Ceiling Balloon Installations"
  description="Ceiling balloon installations in London Ontario. Suspended clusters, canopies, and overhead displays for ballrooms and venues. Installs from $699."
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Services', url: '/services' },
    { name: 'Ceiling installs', url: '/services/ceiling' },
  ]}
  schemas={schemas}
>
  <Hero
    eyebrow="Install type"
    headline="Ceiling balloon installations in London, Ontario"
    subhead="Suspended clusters, canopies, and overhead displays. The install that changes how a whole room feels rather than one wall of it."
    primaryCta={{ href: '/quote', label: 'Start a quote' }}
    secondaryCta={{ href: '/portfolio', label: 'See ceiling work' }}
    image="/images/categories/ceiling.webp"
    imageAlt="Ceiling balloon installation in a ballroom"
    variant="page"
  />

  <section class="install-body section">
    <div class="container container-narrow prose">
      <p>
        Every other install type decorates a wall or a corner. A ceiling install changes the room
        itself. Guests walk in and the space reads differently before they have looked at anything in
        particular, which is why venues and corporate clients ask for it when a room is large and
        otherwise plain. It is also the most technical thing we build, so it rewards booking early.
      </p>

      <h2>What a ceiling balloon installation costs</h2>
      <p>
        Small overhead clusters and floating accents over a head table or bar start around $699. Larger
        canopies and multi-cluster installs across a ballroom run $1,200 to $1,999. Full-room canopies
        and suspended feature pieces reach $2,400 and beyond. This is the highest-ticket category we
        build, and the reason is labour and access rather than materials. Overhead work is measured,
        rigged, and hung piece by piece from a ladder or a lift, and that time is most of the cost.
      </p>

      <h2>What your venue needs to allow</h2>
      <p>
        Three things decide whether a ceiling install is possible, and all three are worth confirming
        before you book rather than on the day. There has to be an attachment point, which usually means
        existing rigging, beams, light bars, or drop ceiling grid. Some venues in London allow fishing
        line and clips, some allow nothing overhead at all, and a few have rigging that only their own
        staff may touch. There has to be access, since anything above roughly twelve feet needs a ladder
        or lift brought in and floor space clear to set it up. And there has to be a setup window with
        the room empty, because this is the one install that cannot happen around guests or around
        another vendor dressing tables underneath.
      </p>
      <p>
        Brenda confirms all of that with the venue coordinator directly, so you are not carrying
        messages between two vendors the week of your event. Tell us the venue name when you enquire and
        there is a good chance we already know their rules.
      </p>

      <h2>Where overhead work earns its cost</h2>
      <p>
        Indoor weddings with height, corporate galas and award banquets, product launches, and large
        milestone parties are where this lands best. In a room with a plain ceiling and good height, an
        overhead install does more than the same budget spent on floor pieces, because it is visible
        from every seat rather than only from the side of the room it sits on. In a low-ceiling room it
        is usually the wrong call, and we will say so rather than sell it to you. If your ceiling is low
        or the venue does not permit overhead work, a
        <a href="/services/walls-backdrops">balloon wall</a> or a tall
        <a href="/services/balloon-arches">arch</a> gets you scale a different way.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because of the rigging and access requirements, book overhead work earlier than other install
        types. Four to six weeks leaves room to confirm venue rules and lock a setup window. Timelines
        are covered in the <a href="/faq">FAQ</a>, and
        <a href="/services/corporate">corporate packages</a> covers recurring venue work and standing
        arrangements.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {products.length > 0 && (
    <section class="install-products section">
      <div class="container">
        <header class="section-head">
          <p class="eyebrow">Shop the catalog</p>
          <h2>Ceiling installs in the catalog</h2>
          <p class="lede">Starting points for a custom overhead build.</p>
        </header>
        <ProductGrid products={products} columns={3} />
        <p class="section-link-wrap">
          <a class="section-link" href="https://shop.balloonia.events/collections/ceiling-installations">View all ceiling installs →</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  )}

  {faqs.length > 0 && <FAQAccordion heading="Ceiling installation questions" faqs={faqs} />}

  <section class="install-quote section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Custom build</p>
        <h2>Planning an overhead install?</h2>
        <p class="lede">Send your venue and ceiling height. Brenda confirms what is possible there and quotes within 24 hours.</p>
      </header>
      <QuoteForm client:load />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .prose p { color: var(--color-ink-soft); font-size: var(--font-size-lg); line-height: var(--line-relaxed); }
  .prose h2 { margin-top: var(--space-6); margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .prose a { color: var(--color-accent-deep); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .section-head { margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .install-quote { background: var(--color-paper-soft); }
  .section-link { color: var(--color-accent-deep); font-size: var(--font-size-sm); font-weight: 500; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 4px; }
  .section-link-wrap { margin-top: var(--space-5); }
</style>
